<h2 class="mt-12">Governance and documentation for food and beverage</h2>
<div class="overflow-x-auto mb-8"><table>
<thead><tr><th>Practice</th><th>Standard</th><th>Risk it prevents</th></tr></thead>
<tbody>
<tr><td>Flow ownership</td><td>One accountable food and beverage operator per flow</td><td>food and beverage ghosts sending expired incentives</td></tr>
<tr><td>Naming convention</td><td>Food And Beverage prefixes by job and audience</td><td>Peak food and beverage triage blind without naming</td></tr>
<tr><td>Change log</td><td>Log food and beverage edits with date and rationale</td><td>Unlogged food and beverage changes hiding causes</td></tr>
<tr><td>Access control</td><td>food and beverage-editor seats minimal by default</td><td>Food And Beverage accidents from excess access</td></tr>
<tr><td>Quarterly flow review</td><td>Prune idle food and beverage branches quarterly</td><td>food and beverage cruft raising edit cost</td></tr>
<tr><td>Incident runbook</td><td>food and beverage break-glass steps pre-written</td><td>Food And Beverage harm airing too long</td></tr>
</tbody></table></div>
<h2 class="mt-12">Peak season readiness for food and beverage</h2>
<ol>
<li>For food and beverage, freeze journey changes two weeks pre-peak.</li>
<li>Food And Beverage QA spans purchase, refund, and case paths.</li>
<li>Verify food and beverage suppression clears recent buyers and open returns.</li>
<li>Enlarge food and beverage holdouts so peak reads stay valid.</li>
<li>Food And Beverage texting policy written before peak.</li>
<li>Food And Beverage billing checked on peak math.</li>
<li>Cover food and beverage complaint and bounce review daily.</li>
<li>For food and beverage, document per-journey retreat steps first.</li>
</ol>
<p>Don't let food and beverage run on memory — set the first quarterly food and beverage review before launch, document suppression, caps, and escalation contacts in week one, and future operators get a food and beverage runbook instead of rumors.</p>
<p>For food and beverage, make the quarterly write-up non-negotiable — shipped, suppressed, margin, misses — because a standing food and beverage evidence base beats recalled anecdotes at renewal time.</p>
